!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SMMC-7721
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: liver cancer
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = m6a antibody: N6-methyladenosine(m6A)(Millipore,ABE572)
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SMMC-7721 cells were cultured under hypoxia(1% O2) for 48 hours in DMEM(Corning, USA) supplemented 10% FBS(Gibco,South America)
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = total RNAs were harvested from SMMC-7721 cells cultured under hypoxia using Trizol reagent, and then were chemically broken into fragments of ~100 nt. The m6A modification of RNAs were isolated with m6A antibody
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were constructed according to the standard manufacture's instruction(NEB Next Ultra RNA library Prep Kit,illumina)
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina Casava1.7 software used for basecalling.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were trimmed for adaptor sequence, and masked for low-complexity or low-quality sequence, then mapped to hg19 whole genome using bowtie v0.12.2 with parameters -p 32 -m 5 --best --strata
!Sample_data_processing = peak calling was conducted using MACS v1.4.2 with the parameters --name --format --gsize --tsize --nomodel --shiftsize -S, and then sort out peaks having an FDR<5%
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab-delimited text file includes m6A abundance of RNAs for sample
